---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout>
	<main class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20">
		<header class="mb-20">
			<h1 class="text-5xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">Sovereign Wealth Infrastructure.</h1>
			<p class="text-2xl text-slate-600 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
				I help individuals and businesses design and implement robust Bitcoin self-custody systems. 
				Engineering precision meets financial security.
			</p>
		</header>

		<section class="mb-20">
			<h2 class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500 font-bold mb-8">Consultancy Philosophy</h2>
			<div class="grid md:grid-cols-2 gap-12 text-slate-700">
				<p>Your Bitcoin is only as secure as the architecture protecting it. I bridge the gap between complex engineering and accessible, resilient custody solutions.</p>
				<p>With a background in software engineering and OTC trading, I bring a unique perspective on threat modeling, asset lifecycle management, and operational security.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<!-- New Educational Content Block -->
		<section class="mb-20">
			<h2 class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500 font-bold mb-8">Latest Insights</h2>
			<div class="space-y-6">
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">EU Regulation</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/mica-phase-2-live-eu-bitcoin-aftermath" class="hover:underline">
							MiCA Phase 2 Is Live: Europe Just Lost 92% of Its Crypto Firms
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						The EU's MiCA transitional period expired on July 1, 2026. Over 2,500 crypto firms are gone.
						Binance exited several countries. USDT got delisted. Here is what the new European crypto
						landscape looks like and what it means for your bitcoin.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/mica-phase-2-live-eu-bitcoin-aftermath" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">&#8594;</span>
					</a>
				</div>
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">Bitcoin Protocol</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/bitcoin-core-31-1-bip-110-protocol-war" class="hover:underline">
							Bitcoin Core 31.1 and BIP-110: Why the Protocol War Is Your Problem
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						Bitcoin Core 31.1 fixes a privacy bug that could leak your IP address. BIP-110, a separate
						proposal heading toward forced activation in August, could invalidate wallet transactions
						built on Miniscript and certain Taproot scripts. Both affect your self-custody setup.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/bitcoin-core-31-1-bip-110-protocol-war" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">&#8594;</span>
					</a>
				</div>
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">Bitcoin Law</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/noah-doe-bitcoin-self-custody-legal-attack" class="hover:underline">
							The Noah Doe Case: Why Self-Custody Is Under Legal Attack
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						A New York lawsuit is asking a court to declare 39,069 dormant Bitcoin addresses as abandoned
						property worth 293 billion dollars, including Satoshi's coins. Here is what the filing does,
						why it is weak, and why it still matters for anyone holding their own keys.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/noah-doe-bitcoin-self-custody-legal-attack" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>

				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">EU Regulation</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/mica-self-custody-eu-bitcoin-survival-guide" class="hover:underline">
							MiCA Made Self-Custody Mandatory: Your EU Bitcoin Survival Guide
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						MiCA took full force in December 2024. The law left self-custody untouched but regulated every
						doorway around it. Here is why the exchange layer is now the risk layer, and what European
						bitcoin holders should do about it.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/mica-self-custody-eu-bitcoin-survival-guide" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">Bitcoin Protocol</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/quantum-bitcoin-post-quantum-upgrade-race" class="hover:underline">
							Quantum Bitcoin: The Post-Quantum Upgrade Race Is Real
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						Two Bitcoin Improvement Proposals landed in eight months and they disagree on the right way forward.
						BIP-360 builds an opt-in quantum-resistant output type. BIP-361 wants a mandatory sunset on the old cryptography.
						One third of all bitcoin has an exposed public key on-chain already.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/quantum-bitcoin-post-quantum-upgrade-race" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">Lightning &amp; Regulation</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/spending-bitcoin-eurozone-after-mica-wavespace-lightning" class="hover:underline">
							Spending Bitcoin in the Eurozone After MiCA: Wavespace and the Lightning Gap
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						The EU's July 1 deadline made custodial Bitcoin slower, more invasive, and harder to spend.
						A small open-source Lightning wallet called Wavespace sits in the gap MiCA deliberately left open —
						outside the regulation, on your phone, with your keys.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/spending-bitcoin-eurozone-after-mica-wavespace-lightning" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">EU Regulation</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/mica-july-1-deadline-self-custody-exemption-what-eu-users-need-to-know" class="hover:underline">
							MiCA's July 1 Deadline Just Passed: What EU Bitcoin Users Actually Need to Know
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						The EU's grandfathering window for crypto exchanges expired on July 1, 2026. Here is what changed,
						what did not, and the one thing the regulation leaves completely untouched — your right to hold your own keys.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/mica-july-1-deadline-self-custody-exemption-what-eu-users-need-to-know" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">Bitcoin Treasury</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/strategys-bitcoin-sales-framework-what-it-means-for-self-custody" class="hover:underline">
							Strategy's Bitcoin Sales Framework: What It Means for Self-Custody
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						The largest corporate holder of Bitcoin just gave itself permission to sell. Why JPMorgan flagged it
						as a new kind of market risk — and why it makes the case for holding your own keys stronger.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/strategys-bitcoin-sales-framework-what-it-means-for-self-custody" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">Privacy Wallet</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/wasabi-2-8-0-and-the-state-of-bitcoin-privacy-wallets-2026" class="hover:underline">
							Wasabi 2.8.0 and the State of Bitcoin Privacy Wallets in 2026
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						Wasabi's biggest release in years kills its own backend, pays inside coinjoins, and edges toward full
						network sovereignty. Here is what changed, why it matters, and where privacy wallets still fall short.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/wasabi-2-8-0-and-the-state-of-bitcoin-privacy-wallets-2026" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
				<div class="p-8 border border-slate-200 rounded-2xl hover:border-slate-400 transition-colors">
					<span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-amber-500 mb-2 block">Hardware Review</span>
					<h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-3">
						<a href="/insights/why-your-next-hardware-wallet-should-have-a-keyboard" class="hover:underline">
							Why Your Next Hardware Wallet Needs a QWERTY Keyboard — Coldcard Q Review
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600 mb-6 leading-relaxed">
						Entering passphrases on a 12-key numeric pad is more than just painful—it is an operational vulnerability.
						Here is how Coinkite's physical powerhouse changes the self-custody equation.
					</p>
					<a href="/insights/why-your-next-hardware-wallet-should-have-a-keyboard" class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 group">
						Read Article <span class="group-hover:translate-x-1 transition-transform">→</span>
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="mb-20">
			<h2 class="text-sm uppercase tracking-widest text-slate-500 font-bold mb-8">Services</h2>
			<div class="space-y-6">
				<div class="border-l-2 border-slate-300 pl-6">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-lg">Self-Custody Architecture</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600">Custom multi-signature setups, hardware security module integration, and cold storage planning.</p>
				</div>
				<div class="border-l-2 border-slate-300 pl-6">
					<h3 class="font-bold text-lg">Security Auditing</h3>
					<p class="text-slate-600">Reviewing your current infrastructure for single points of failure and operational vulnerabilities.</p>
				</div>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
			<a href="https://cal.com/banitama/15min" class="block p-8 border border-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-50 transition-colors">
				<h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Book Consultation</h3>
				<p class="text-xs uppercase text-slate-500">Secure Strategy Session</p>
			</a>
			<a href="https://t.me/your-handle" class="block p-8 border border-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-50 transition-colors">
				<h3 class="font-bold mb-1">Telegram</h3>
				<p class="text-xs uppercase text-slate-500">Encrypted Messaging</p>
			</a>
			<a href="https://wa.me/your-number" class="block p-8 border border-slate-200 hover:bg-slate-50 transition-colors">
				<h3 class="font-bold mb-1">WhatsApp</h3>
				<p class="text-xs uppercase text-slate-500">Direct Contact</p>
			</a>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
